.\" Manpage for castmirror. Apache-2.0. See NOTICE for the GPL implications of
.\" distributing a binary linked against libx264.
.TH CASTMIRROR 1 "2026-11-18" "CastMirror 1.0.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
castmirror \- send a display or window to a Google Cast receiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B castmirror
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B castmirror
is the interactive and flag-driven command line front end to the CastMirror
core. It discovers Google Cast, Android TV and Nest receivers on the local
network, captures a display or a single window, encodes H.264 (VAAPI, Media
Foundation or FFmpeg libx264) or VP8 video and Opus audio, and streams the
result over the Cast Streaming protocol (CAST/CST2 RTP over UDP with compound
RTCP).
.PP
Run with no options to enter the interactive prompt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-device " <IP or ID>"
Target receiver by IP address or Cast device UUID. Implies non-interactive mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-display " <ID>"
Display or monitor index to capture. Default is saved config (0 initially).
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-window .
.TP
.BI \-\-window " <ID>"
Share a single window, identified by its numeric window ID (X11 XID on Linux,
HWND integer on Windows). Use
.B \-\-list-windows
to enumerate IDs. Requires
.B \-\-device
when starting a stream.
.TP
.B \-\-list-windows
List capturable windows and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-displays
List available displays and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " <preset>"
Quality preset (case-insensitive): Auto, High, Balanced, Smooth, Game or Cinema.
Default is saved config (Auto initially). Game requests a 150 ms target
playout delay and locks resolution; Cinema requests 400 ms.
.TP
.B \-\-no-audio
Disable audio mirroring for this session.
.TP
.BI \-\-bitrate " <kbps>"
Custom video bitrate ceiling in kilobits per second (1\-100000).
.TP
.BI \-\-codec " <h264|vp8>"
Select the video codec (h264 or vp8). Default is saved config (h264 initially).
.TP
.B \-\-low-latency
Force a 200 ms target playout delay.
.TP
.B \-\-no-verify
Bypass Cast device certificate verification. Development escape hatch; do not
use it on an untrusted network.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth-probe " <IP>"
Connect to a device, run the device authentication challenge and exit. Honors
.BR \-\-no-verify .
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show the help message and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
When invoked without
.BR \-\-device ,
.BR \-\-window ,
.BR \-\-auth-probe ,
.BR \-\-list-windows ,
or
.BR \-\-list-displays ,
.B castmirror
scans for Cast devices and opens an interactive menu:
.TP
.BI 1 \- N
Select discovered device
.I N
and start casting the configured display.
.TP
.B L
Cast to the last used device.
.TP
.B P
Cycle the quality preset (Auto, High, Balanced, Smooth, Game, Cinema) and save.
.TP
.B M
Toggle audio mirroring and save.
.TP
.B A
Add a Cast device manually by IPv4 address.
.TP
.B W
Cast a single window by ID (shown when window capture is supported).
.TP
.B R
Refresh / rescan for Cast devices.
.TP
.B Q
Quit.
.PP
While streaming, press
.B Enter
or send
.B SIGINT
/
.B SIGTERM
(Ctrl+C) to stop cleanly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested work completed.
.TP
.B 1
The cast could not be started, a connection failed, or
.B \-\-auth-probe
failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was not understood (usage error).
.TP
.B 3
The session started but ended in failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_FORCE_SOFTWARE_ENCODE=1
Force FFmpeg libx264 software encoding even where VAAPI or Media Foundation
hardware encoding is available.
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_VAAPI_DEVICE=/dev/dri/renderD129
Linux only: use a specific VAAPI render node instead of probing
.IR /dev/dri/renderD* .
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_FORCE_X11=1
Linux only: force X11 capture instead of the Wayland xdg-desktop-portal
ScreenCast path.
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_CONFIG_DIR=/path/to/dir
Read and write
.I config.json
and log files in this directory instead of the default per-user location.
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_VERBOSE_JSON=1
Enable structured NDJSON diagnostic breadcrumbs in
.IR castmirror.ndjson .
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_ALLOW_SYNTHETIC_CAPTURE=1
Allow synthetic generated video/audio when real display capture is unavailable
(intended for automated tests).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/config.json
Persisted settings (on Windows:
.IR %APPDATA%\eCastMirror\econfig.json ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/castmirror.log
Rotating engine log.
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/castmirror-session.log
Per-session debug log overwritten on each cast.
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/castmirror.ndjson
Structured NDJSON diagnostics when
.B CASTMIRROR_VERBOSE_JSON=1
or
.B verbose_json_logging
is enabled.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
castmirror \-\-device 192.168.1.150 \-\-display 0 \-\-preset High
castmirror \-\-device 192.168.1.150 \-\-no-audio
castmirror \-\-list-windows
castmirror \-\-auth-probe 192.168.1.150
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR castmirror-gui (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR pactl (1)
.SH NOTES
Distributing a compiled CastMirror binary linked against GPL-licensed libx264
generally requires treating that binary as GPL. See the NOTICE file shipped
